"""
Trading system with order-type support.

The design intentionally centralizes order-type-specific behavior behind a
single `OrderTypeHandler` interface (Strategy pattern) that is registered in
an `OrderTypeRegistry`. Every subsystem (validation, routing, execution,
risk, position tracking, settlement, compliance, reporting, audit, and the
client API) queries the registry instead of embedding per-order-type
branching logic. Adding a new order type therefore requires exactly ONE new
handler class + one registration call, instead of touching 20+ files.

This file is organized into logical sections (as if they were separate
modules) to show how each subsystem plugs into the registry.
"""

